  "scope": "Accept the explicit version3.3.0 curriculum migration: period16 has7 quarter-turns,2 diagonal reflections and7 ordinary transforms; every five-pair window retains a quarter-turn under each four-demo holdout. Named blue-corner and inverse rivals are taught, with intended frequency/keyed-stream changes rather than a false byte-equivalence claim. Reviewer reports12/12 final battery,119 task tests repeated in fresh replay,300 lessons/1500 holdouts with1500 distinct inputs,48 fixed-seed lessons/240 holdouts with60 distinct inputs.480 valid class strings and80 fallback holdouts checked;30 representatives do not imply uniform rejection-sampled support. Collision probe examines5120 inputs,4096 overlapping windows,20480 events; only10 retained witness inputs are Racket-labelled. It refutes one specified projection at each holdout, not all schedule leakage. Forward/inverse prototype:8 quarter-turn-only episodes,40 holdouts,90 Racket calls,8 canonical records/four distinct pairs;16 actual emitted file hashes checked. Canonical Racket unchanged. Broader suite remains FAIL:19 failed,1000 passed,3 skipped,18 subtests, not all failures baseline-reproduced. Final solve consulted own prior Python, so is exposed and not independent; mixed-source prior executions remain separate. No variant or trajectory admission. File/source/public-private checks performed statically; all runtime/test measurements remain reviewer-reported.",
